# Intent: Train 5 measurement. A bench build counts screen refreshes and flushed pixels (one WARN line "FACEFPS ..." every 10 seconds) and adds four tools: self.face.bench_fps (the draw rate since the last call: refreshes a second, full-frame equivalents, average refresh time, passes of the update loop, the peak second and the mean over the seconds that drew at least 5 times), self.face.bench_run (a repeatable workload of at most 25 seconds, because a tool that runs 30 s on the main loop makes the unit restart itself: idle, talk with a synthetic speech level, move, emotions), self.face.bench_speak (hold the speaking look and a steady speech level in the background) and self.face.snapshot (the screen as LVGL draws it, written on the USB cable as '@snap <row> <hex>' lines, which scripts/fw-serial.py turns into a PNG so a screen nobody can see can still be looked at). It also lets the USB cable reader take lines of up to 4096 characters (it took 512), so a picture piece fits on one line. Off in every shipped image: no counter, no tool, no code.
